<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37588" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξορίζω</span></b>  (A), (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅρος</span>) (3sg.
		aor.
		subj.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξορύξη</span> [from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐξορϝίξ-</span>] <i><span class="en">
			<u>Inscr.Cypr.</u>
			135.11
		</span></i> H.):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>send
				beyond the frontier, banish,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Heracl.</u>
				257
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				874a
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γᾶθέν τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					1106
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ σῶμά τινος ἐ.</span>
			(cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξόριστος</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Phoc.</u>
				37
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξορισθῆναι καὶ ἀποθανόντα, μηδὲ ἐν
					τῇ πατρίδι ταφῆναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hyp.
					<u>Lyc.</u>
					20
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>expose</i> a child, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ion</u>
				504
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>banish, get rid of,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγριότητα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					197d
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰσχρολογίαν ἐκ τῆς πόλεως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1336b5
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς ἀνιάτους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>EN</u>
					1180a10
				</span></i>
			: c. gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τι τῆς ἀκοῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
					<u>Or.</u>
					6.186b
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> c. acc. loci
			only, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλλην ἀπ᾽ ἄλλης ἐ. πόλιν</span>
			<i>pass</i> from one to another, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Heracl.</u>
				16
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>come forth from,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Hipp.</u>
					1380
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.).</div>
